.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt VT 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vt
.Nd virtual terminal layer for the kernel text console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device vt"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
layer provides the kernel text console's virtual terminals.
Each VT maintains its own screen buffer, cursor state, ANSI parser state,
scrollback history, and attached
.Xr tty 4
instance.
.Pp
The active VT is displayed through the VGA hardware text backend.
Inactive VTs retain their state in memory and are redrawn when activated.
.Pp
Printable characters and escape sequences are interpreted through a shared
VT102/ANSI parser, but the parser state itself is maintained per VT so that
cursor position, saved state, and pending sequence parameters survive console
switches.
.Pp
Substrate currently provides:
.Bl -bullet
.It
12 virtual terminals
.It
dedicated
.Pa /dev/tty1
through
.Pa /dev/tty12
devices
.It
.Li Alt+F1
through
.Li Alt+F12
for console switching
.It
per-VT scrollback, entered with
.Li Shift+PageUp
and left with
.Li Shift+PageDown
.It
VT102 scroll margins
.Pq DECSTBM
for region-limited insert, delete, and scroll operations
.It
16-color foreground and background attributes through the VGA text palette
.It
a kernel-owned status line on the last physical text row
.El
.Pp
Scrollback freezes the visible console view while live output continues to
append to the active VT buffer. The status line shows the current VT number and
the number of lines by which the view is scrolled back.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/sys/drivers/console/vt.c"
.It Pa /sys/drivers/console/vt.c
VT state management and scrollback logic.
.It Pa /sys/include/sys/vt.h
VT data structures and interface.
.It Pa /sys/drivers/video/hw_text.c
VGA hardware text backend.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr keyboard 4 ,
.Xr tty 4
